From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <fardjad.davari2@jumbo.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 08:11:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: configure session picker default filter

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Let users choose the initial /resume picker filter.
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 1003-personal-feature-configure-session-picker-sorting.patch

Patch intent:
Add display.session_picker_default_filter with all and current-dir modes.
Apply it when /resume opens so the picker can start scoped to the current
working directory instead of always listing every session.

Why it exists:
The picker always opened on All sessions, forcing users in multi-project
directories to press s every time to reach the current-dir filter they
already use.

Upstream integration points:
DisplayConfig gains session_picker_default_filter next to
session_picker_sort. SessionPicker::apply_configured_default_filter maps
the config to SessionFilterMode and is called after set_current_dir in
both open_session_picker and the async Resume fallback in
apply_loaded_session_picker.

Update guidance:
Preserve all as the default. Route every new picker entry point through
apply_configured_default_filter after the working directory is recorded so
the CurrentDir filter has the comparison base it needs.

Validation:
cargo test -p jcode-config-types session_picker_sort_defaults_to_recent_and_accepts_named_orders --lib
cargo test -p jcode-tui test_filter_mode_keyboard_shortcuts_cycle_both_directions --lib
